🚀 Getting Started

Prerequisites

- Node.js (LTS recommended)
- npm
- Git

Installation

Clone your repository:

git clone YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
cd YOUR_REPOSITORY_FOLDER

Install dependencies:

npm install

Start the development server:

npm run dev

Create a production build:

npm run build

Run available checks:

npm run

Use the scripts listed in "package.json" for testing and linting.

⌨️ Keyboard Shortcuts

Shortcut| Action
"Ctrl/Cmd + N"| Create a note
"Ctrl/Cmd + K"| Focus search
"Ctrl/Cmd + S"| Save changes
"Escape"| Close a dialog or exit an applicable interaction
"Tab" / "Shift + Tab"| Navigate controls

Shortcuts depend on the implemented application version.

💾 Data Storage

Notes are stored locally in the browser.

- No account is required for local use.
- Clearing browser data can remove locally stored notes.
- LocalStorage is not a cloud backup.
- Cross-device synchronization requires an additional backend or synchronization service.

Recommendation: Export and back up important notes before clearing browser data or changing storage implementations.

🔐 Security

- Sanitize rendered Markdown.
- Block unsafe links and script execution.
- Validate stored data before loading it.
- Handle storage failures without reporting false save success.
- Keep private notes and credentials out of public repositories.

